import{_ as r,o as t,c as a,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BZO4qERu.js";const h=JSON.parse('{"title":"Data sources","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/sources.md","filePath":"guide/sources.md","lastUpdated":1792570296000}'),s={name:"guide/sources.md"};function n(i,e,d,c,l,u){return t(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="data-sources" tabindex="-1">Data sources <a class="header-anchor" href="#data-sources" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Data sources&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Choose an index that fits your research. Coverage, metadata, access, and filters vary across providers.</p><h2 id="source-directory" tabindex="-1">Source directory <a class="header-anchor" href="#source-directory" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Source directory&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Community</th><th>Online BYOK</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://openalex.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenAlex</a></td><td>Key recommended</td><td>Key required</td><td>Broad discovery and citation expansion</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://arxiv.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">arXiv</a></td><td>No key</td><td>No key</td><td>Scientific preprints</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.crossref.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Crossref</a></td><td>No key</td><td>No key</td><td>DOI and publication metadata</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.semanticscholar.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Semantic Scholar</a></td><td>Optional key</td><td>Key required</td><td>Papers and scholarly graph metadata</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">PubMed</a></td><td>Optional NCBI key</td><td>Key required</td><td>Biomedical and life-science research</td></tr><tr><td>Google Scholar via <a href="https://serper.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Serper</a></td><td>Serper key required</td><td>Key required</td><td>Scholar results through the supported API</td></tr><tr><td>PaperHub top CS conferences</td><td>No key</td><td>No key</td><td>PaperHub&#39;s conference collection</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://developer.clarivate.com/apis/wos-starter" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Web of Science Starter</a></td><td>Clarivate key required</td><td>Key required</td><td>Supported WoS collection when enabled</td></tr></tbody></table><p>PaperSeek Service manages source access for you. Community permits anonymous access or optional keys as shown above. Online BYOK has a separate access policy: add and save source keys in Settings for every source that takes a key, including OpenAlex, PubMed, and Semantic Scholar. arXiv, Crossref, and PaperHub need no key. A model key is not a data-source key.</p><h2 id="configure-and-test-a-source" tabindex="-1">Configure and test a source <a class="header-anchor" href="#configure-and-test-a-source" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Configure and test a source&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Open <strong>Settings → Data sources</strong> and choose <strong>Configure</strong> or <strong>Configure key</strong> on the source row. Enter the key and options, then click <strong>Save</strong>.</p><p><strong>Test connection</strong> inside this dialog also saves the current key and options before testing. If saving fails, the test does not start. Once saving succeeds, a failed test or subsequently cancelling the dialog does not undo it; reopen the source configuration to change or clear the saved key. The table&#39;s <strong>Test</strong> and <strong>Test all</strong> use the configured credentials without saving a form draft. Model connection draft tests do not save; see <a href="./models">models and ranking</a>.</p><h2 id="obtain-credentials" tabindex="-1">Obtain credentials <a class="header-anchor" href="#obtain-credentials" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Obtain credentials&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><a href="https://openalex.org/settings/api" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">OpenAlex API settings</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.semanticscholar.org/product/api#api-key-form" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Semantic Scholar key request</a>.</li><li><a href="https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK25497/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">NCBI API guidance</a>.</li><li><a href="https://serper.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Serper account</a>.</li><li><a href="https://developer.clarivate.com/apis/wos-starter" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">WoS Starter application</a>.</li></ul><p>Provider subscriptions and rate limits are separate from PaperSeek accounts and credits.</p><h2 id="empty-results-and-temporary-failures" tabindex="-1">Empty results and temporary failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#empty-results-and-temporary-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Empty results and temporary failures&quot;">​</a></h2><p>When a search returns no papers, PaperSeek tries up to two more queries. Each one uses the earlier queries and their counts, and source feedback such as PubMed&#39;s unrecognized phrases, to adjust terminology or optional restrictions. Before a query runs, a separate model check must confirm that it keeps the core concepts, required relationships, and explicit constraints. This check is not a guarantee of relevance; inspect the search process and returned papers. If no suitable query passes, the source still has no matches, or the source cannot be reached for a follow-up query, the search ends with no papers and a notice explaining why, instead of silently dropping required conditions. Field filters remain applied.</p><p>While refining any search, a proposed query that was already run is sent back to the model once, with its earlier result, before refinement stops.</p><p>Rate limits and malformed API responses are reported as source problems, not zero matches. Requests use bounded retries and respect <code>Retry-After</code>; ordinary failures are retried after about a second, rate limits after a longer pause. All tasks running in one PaperSeek process share pacing and cooldowns for the same source and credential, including retries. arXiv, for example, receives one request every three seconds however many searches are running. Semantic Scholar&#39;s bulk-search cooldown does not block ordinary relevance search. Existing candidates survive later query or pagination failures, and unavailable supplementary lanes produce warnings. Separate worker processes or other applications using the same provider account still share the upstream quota, so a retry cannot guarantee availability.</p><h2 id="network-proxy" tabindex="-1">Network proxy <a class="header-anchor" href="#network-proxy" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Network proxy&quot;">​</a></h2><p>If your network cannot reach a source or model provider directly, or a source has throttled your network address, set up a proxy in <strong>Settings › Data sources › Network proxy</strong>. You choose which requests go through it: model requests, sources that limit by network address (arXiv, Crossref, PaperHub, and PubMed or OpenAlex without a key), and other sources. A proxy does not raise a key&#39;s quota. See <a href="./../reference/configuration#network-proxy">Network proxy</a> for the details and the matching environment variables.</p><h2 id="fields-and-categories" tabindex="-1">Fields and categories <a class="header-anchor" href="#fields-and-categories" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Fields and categories&quot;">​</a></h2><p>OpenAlex uses supported discipline options; its semantic lane applies supported filtering behavior. arXiv uses categories. WoS categories and the WoS database selector are separate. Other sources use textual field guidance.</p><p>Restricting a field can exclude interdisciplinary work. Start without it unless your research design requires the constraint.</p><h2 id="missing-metadata" tabindex="-1">Missing metadata <a class="header-anchor" href="#missing-metadata" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Missing metadata&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Records can lack abstracts, years, citation counts, or open PDF links. Missing metadata is not a quality judgment.</p><p>Version 1.0.0-beta4 has no separate cross-source abstract-filling or citation-count enrichment switch. Choose informative abstracts for review writing.</p><h2 id="multiple-keys" tabindex="-1">Multiple keys <a class="header-anchor" href="#multiple-keys" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Multiple keys&quot;">​</a></h2><p>OpenAlex and Serper support key pools separated by whitespace, commas, or semicolons. Requests rotate the starting key; authentication failures are handled separately from transient errors.</p><p>Rotation does not change provider terms or guarantee remaining credit. See <a href="./../reference/configuration">configuration</a>.</p>',26)])])}const f=r(s,[["render",n]]);export{h as __pageData,f as default};
